  "upstream": [],
  "delta": [
    "Freeze the durable `erasure` event payload after the P25 header/payload split: targets, erased versions, erased event refs with retained digests, and uncovered session references.",
    "An erased event keeps its header, sequence, id, type and SHA-256 payload digest; only the payload bytes are cleared, so the audit record can prove what was removed without reconstructing it.",
    "S6 step 2 adds the host-only closed-session rewrite (§4.6, P02 wal.md §5.3): a durable erasure names the tombstoned `record://session/...` refs and the switched session epochs; only genuinely active sessions stay in `uncoveredRecords`."
  ],
